MULATION of a screen capture, not a real one. Every other transform in this battery is applied to real signed bytes by a real encoder; this one models what a screenshot does rather than taking one. It is labelled so the distinction travels with the result. (The modelling is conservative: a real screenshot discards the container entirely, so it cannot preserve a manifest that this simulation destroys.)","name":"screenshot_equiv"},{"description":"JPEG -> PNG","name":"format_convert_png"},{"description":"JPEG -> WebP q90","name":"format_convert_webp"},{"description":"JPEG -> HEIC (no encoder available)","name":"format_convert_heic"}],"unmeasured_reasons":{"format_convert_heic":"TransformUnavailable: no HEIF encoder: KeyError: 'HEIF'"},"version":"0.1.0"}